From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 01:05:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtl837x: address all indexed hardware tables

Include the caller-supplied index for all non-L2 table accesses. The former CVLAN-only branch caused ACL rule and action requests to access entry zero regardless of their requested index.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/rtl837x_table.c
+++ b/src/rtl837x_table.c
@@ -68,12 +68,11 @@ int rtl837x_ita_execute(struct realtek_p
 		} else {
 			write_data = true;
 		}
-	} else if (table == RTL837X_TABLE_CVLAN) {
+	} else {
+		/* All non-L2 tables are indexed, including both ACL halves. */
 		cmd |= FIELD_PREP(RTL837X_TABLE_CTRL_ADDR_MASK, *addr);
 		if (opera == RTL837X_TABLE_OPERA_WRITE)
 			write_data = true;
-	} else if (opera == RTL837X_TABLE_OPERA_WRITE) {
-		write_data = true;
 	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&priv->map_lock);
